{"page":552,"blocks":[{"x":0.04849,"y":0.05257,"w":0.34069,"h":0.01535,"fs":0.01535,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"538 Chapter 9: First-Order Differential Equations"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.09309,"w":0.16102,"h":0.01365,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Solution The equation"},{"x":0.57846,"y":0.11408,"w":0.07868,"h":0.02973,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"dy dx = y - x"},{"x":0.32333,"y":0.15376,"w":0.37615,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"is a first-order differential equation with ƒ(x, y) = y - x."},{"x":0.35277,"y":0.18512,"w":0.2072,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"On the left side of the equation:"},{"x":0.53265,"y":0.20449,"w":0.10045,"h":0.0305,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"dx ax + 1 - 1"},{"x":0.62491,"y":0.20449,"w":0.11801,"h":0.03035,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"3exb = 1 - 1 3ex."},{"x":0.49274,"y":0.20526,"w":0.05171,"h":0.02973,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"dy dx = d"},{"x":0.10494,"y":0.23543,"w":0.17607,"h":0.02675,"fs":0.01023,"n":6,"k":0,"t":"y = (x + 1) − ex 1 3 a b"},{"x":0.35277,"y":0.24561,"w":0.21812,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"On the right side of the equation:"},{"x":0.10773,"y":0.24654,"w":0.0225,"h":0.02144,"fs":0.01023,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"0, 2 3"},{"x":0.47941,"y":0.26839,"w":0.1464,"h":0.01982,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"y - x = (x + 1) - 1"},{"x":0.61763,"y":0.26839,"w":0.13908,"h":0.02695,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"3ex - x = 1 - 1 3ex."},{"x":0.05706,"y":0.28125,"w":0.19562,"h":0.01078,"fs":0.01023,"n":4,"k":0,"t":"−4 −2 2 4"},{"x":0.13878,"y":0.29082,"w":0.01745,"h":0.01078,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"−1"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.30612,"w":0.32864,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"The function satisfies the initial condition because"},{"x":0.13878,"y":0.30741,"w":0.01745,"h":0.01078,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"−2"},{"x":0.13878,"y":0.32399,"w":0.01745,"h":0.01078,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"−3"},{"x":0.47318,"y":0.32548,"w":0.14247,"h":0.02323,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"y(0) = c (x + 1) - 1"},{"x":0.60748,"y":0.32548,"w":0.05184,"h":0.0337,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"3exd x=0"},{"x":0.66667,"y":0.32888,"w":0.05778,"h":0.01982,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"= 1 - 1"},{"x":0.71626,"y":0.32888,"w":0.04666,"h":0.02695,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"3 = 2 3."},{"x":0.13878,"y":0.34058,"w":0.01745,"h":0.01078,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"−4"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.36661,"w":0.32083,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"The graph of the function is shown in Figure 9.1."},{"x":0.04849,"y":0.36715,"w":0.23841,"h":0.02762,"fs":0.01151,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"FIGURE 9.1 Graph of the solution to the initial value problem in Example 2."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.40334,"w":0.28871,"h":0.01375,"fs":0.01375,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Slope Fields: Viewing Solution Curves"},{"x":0.32331,"y":0.42731,"w":0.59312,"h":0.15159,"fs":0.01279,"n":10,"k":1,"t":"Each time we specify an initial condition y(x0) = y0 for the solution of a differential equa- tion y′ = ƒ(x, y), the solution curve (graph of the solution) is required to pass through the point (x0, y0) and to have slope ƒ(x0, y0) there. We can picture these slopes graphically by drawing short line segments of slope ƒ(x, y) at selected points (x, y) in the region of the xy-plane that constitutes the domain of ƒ. Each segment has the same slope as the solution curve through (x, y) and so is tangent to the curve there. The resulting picture is called a slope field (or direction field) and gives a visualization of the general shape of the solu- tion curves. Figure 9.2a shows a slope field, with a particular solution sketched into it in Figure 9.2b. We see how these line segments indicate the direction the solution curve takes at each point it passes through."},{"x":0.50032,"y":0.60562,"w":0.27162,"h":0.02144,"fs":0.01023,"n":6,"k":0,"t":"y y 0, 2 3 a b"},{"x":0.60846,"y":0.69679,"w":0.22844,"h":0.01023,"fs":0.01023,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"x x"},{"x":0.40161,"y":0.70291,"w":0.19166,"h":0.01078,"fs":0.01023,"n":5,"k":0,"t":"0 2 −2 −4 4"},{"x":0.62423,"y":0.70291,"w":0.19167,"h":0.01078,"fs":0.01023,"n":5,"k":0,"t":"0 2 −2 −4 4"},{"x":0.48352,"y":0.73052,"w":0.01745,"h":0.01078,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"−2"},{"x":0.70616,"y":0.73052,"w":0.01745,"h":0.01078,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"−2"},{"x":0.48352,"y":0.76433,"w":0.01745,"h":0.01078,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"−4"},{"x":0.70616,"y":0.76434,"w":0.01745,"h":0.01078,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"−4"},{"x":0.49626,"y":0.7864,"w":0.23785,"h":0.01023,"fs":0.01023,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"(a) (b)"},{"x":0.4016,"y":0.80825,"w":0.21757,"h":0.02048,"fs":0.01151,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"FIGURE 9.2 (a) Slope field for dy"},{"x":0.60531,"y":0.81661,"w":0.21588,"h":0.0189,"fs":0.01151,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx = y - x. (b) The particular solu-"},{"x":0.40159,"y":0.83852,"w":0.20044,"h":0.02091,"fs":0.01151,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"tion curve through the point a0, 2"},{"x":0.59467,"y":0.83852,"w":0.0982,"h":0.02761,"fs":0.01151,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"3b (Example 2)."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.89212,"w":0.5929,"h":0.04348,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"Figure 9.3 shows three slope fields and we see how the solution curves behave by fol- lowing the tangent line segments in these fields. Slope fields are useful because they dis- play the overall behavior of the family of solution curves for a given differential equation."}]}